Question 12
The following code is presented in if-else if-else.
```java
int w = Integer.parseInt(jTextField1.getText());
int pay = 0;
if (w == 5)
    pay = w * 20;
else if (w == 8)
    pay = w * 26;
else if (w == 20)
    pay = w * 138;
else if (w == 30)
    pay = 14000;
else
    pay = 0;
```
Convert the code into equivalent `switch` case without affecting the output.

questions.answer:
**Model Solution:**
```java
int w = Integer.parseInt(jTextField1.getText());
int pay = 0;
switch (w) {
    case 5:
        pay = w * 20;
        break;
    case 8:
        pay = w * 26;
        break;
    case 20:
        pay = w * 138;
        break;
    case 30:
        pay = 14000;
        break;
    default:
        pay = 0;
        break;
}
```

